\f0\b \cf0 4. Portability
\f1\b0 \
The binary uses 
\f0\b Little Endian
\f1\b0  byte order (via 
\f2\fs26 to_le_bytes
\f1\fs24 ), ensuring that data stored on an ARM processor (like a Raspberry Pi) can be read on an x86 processor (Intel/AMD) without corruption.\
